WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.672
Most early control-flow errors are structural rather than mathematical.

00:00:04.672 --> 00:00:10.572
A single equals sign assigns a value; double equals compares values.

00:00:10.572 --> 00:00:14.242
If statements need a colon at the end of the condition.

00:00:14.242 --> 00:00:18.385
The lines controlled by the statement must be indented consistently.

00:00:19.183 --> 00:00:25.425
A useful debugging trick is to read the code out loud: “If this is true, do this; otherwise,

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:32.934
do that.” If the spoken logic sounds wrong, the code probably needs attention too.
